[{:db/id "q-276366/field-1/5d01f8da83672028f812de7def6c9ab26a7e2949333115537a6343b596845753" :answer/id #uuid "fade9da3-6839-5bee-8e8f-b7b7dca2365a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.9861" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-276366/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "84559470-63b9-5bc2-b828-9ef9d91e350b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-276366/field-1/5d01f8da83672028f812de7def6c9ab26a7e2949333115537a6343b596845753" :answer-field/choices ["q-276366/field-1/5d01f8da83672028f812de7def6c9ab26a7e2949333115537a6343b596845753"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-276366" :question/id #uuid "f7729064-d321-5d9e-a76a-26a9ede41654" :question/math-academy-id "q-276366" :question/problem "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $X∼N(-2,{5}^{2}),$ compute $P(X<9).$ Use the table below and do not round your answer.\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.00\\,$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,2.0\\,$ | $\\,0.9772\\,$ | $\\,0.9778\\,$ | $\\,0.9783\\,$ |\n| $\\,2.1\\,$ | $\\,0.9821\\,$ | $\\,0.9826\\,$ | $\\,0.9830\\,$ |\n| $\\,2.2\\,$ | $\\,0.9861\\,$ | $\\,0.9864\\,$ | $\\,0.9868\\,$ |\n\n$P(X<9)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Given a normal random variable $X∼N(\\mu ,{\\sigma }^{2}),$ we have\n\n$$\nP(X<x)=P(Z<\\frac{x-\\mu }{\\sigma })\n$$\n\nwhere $Z∼N(0,1)$ is a standard normal random variable. In our case, we have $\\mu =-2$ and $\\sigma =5.$\n\nFirst, we transform $X$ into a standard normal random variable $Z$ by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<9) & =P(Z<\\frac{9-(-2)}{5}) \\\\  & =P(Z<2.2) \\\\  & =P(Z\\le 2.2) \\\\  & =Φ(2.2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070250/assets/8ac4c36c58d5189e2483a71e2b0dbbe8e629dd9537d90b2338000d36915880a1.png)\n\nAccording to the table, we have\n\n$$\nΦ(2.2)=0.9861.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\nP(X<9)=0.9861.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-276366/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "98bd56e8-77ca-553a-9c26-04feae0618dd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-276366"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-94247/selection/c526c0533b3f6a935d15b95b994ef7a0a09c39f2ce1735761aaf27f397ce2069" :answer/id #uuid "ca942e0b-78e2-50fe-983f-5da83b66adb5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.2266" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94247/selection/c1a402a8b71b8d948591febfab0a0a7534e7079b0bf1d5ec57b94e5962df969a" :answer/id #uuid "50f239fe-3c7c-52dc-a221-d8b77cac1131" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.2236" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94247/selection/be4645e03d2c05d0337078965cf2cb75615e664fff734b1dfc355dc28d8df951" :answer/id #uuid "57530476-73aa-5718-8351-01f62053d98f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.2578" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94247/selection/44db1682146f8010ea3914483b7e35049681ad551a30679bd9a71878da99fbc8" :answer/id #uuid "863dbeb1-d661-55cd-891f-f9e9ea43c8fc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.2546" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94247/selection/0d074323c126a95f5a468b0c107f571c6fe0b50e406fc2a8002cce19924dedae" :answer/id #uuid "35ea7e91-2d5e-53bd-94a0-544932d5d240" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.2514" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94247/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8d113680-9a34-5bda-a786-a3e6f5237b3a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-94247/selection/c1a402a8b71b8d948591febfab0a0a7534e7079b0bf1d5ec57b94e5962df969a" :answer-field/choices ["q-94247/selection/c526c0533b3f6a935d15b95b994ef7a0a09c39f2ce1735761aaf27f397ce2069" "q-94247/selection/c1a402a8b71b8d948591febfab0a0a7534e7079b0bf1d5ec57b94e5962df969a" "q-94247/selection/be4645e03d2c05d0337078965cf2cb75615e664fff734b1dfc355dc28d8df951" "q-94247/selection/44db1682146f8010ea3914483b7e35049681ad551a30679bd9a71878da99fbc8" "q-94247/selection/0d074323c126a95f5a468b0c107f571c6fe0b50e406fc2a8002cce19924dedae"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-94247" :question/id #uuid "d522427b-b990-5c13-9935-456f89f8489e" :question/math-academy-id "q-94247" :question/problem "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $X∼N(-2,{3}^{2}),$ compute $P(X<-4.28).$\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ | $\\,0.06\\,$ | $\\,0.07\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,-0.8\\,$ | $\\,0.1977\\,$ | $\\,0.1949\\,$ | $\\,0.1922\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.7\\,$ | $\\,0.2266\\,$ | $\\,0.2236\\,$ | $\\,0.2206\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.6\\,$ | $\\,0.2578\\,$ | $\\,0.2546\\,$ | $\\,0.2514\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "Given a normal random variable $X∼N(\\mu ,{\\sigma }^{2}),$ we have\n\n$$\nP(X<x)=P(Z<\\frac{x-\\mu }{\\sigma })\n$$\n\nwhere $Z∼N(0,1)$ is a standard normal random variable. In our case, we have $\\mu =-2$ and $\\sigma =3.$\n\nFirst, we transform $X$ into a standard normal random variable $Z$ by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<-4.28) & =P(Z<\\frac{-4.28-(-2)}{3}) \\\\  & =P(Z<-0.76) \\\\  & =P(Z\\le -0.76) \\\\  & =Φ(-0.76)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070250/assets/56f9956d27f7527106869001273833c863d26053baf8c624c98d4ec2fb3c7f7b.png)\n\nAccording to the table, we have\n\n$$\nΦ(-0.76)=0.2236.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\nP(X<-4.28)=0.2236.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-94247/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "98bd56e8-77ca-553a-9c26-04feae0618dd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-94247"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-276764/field-1/75d591cab066a89426c20e8dd31ecca8224da9661d1e56a33a0e42f85d2e1846" :answer/id #uuid "c51da754-fb65-5307-b8b5-7418b854969f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.3085" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-276764/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "c03948c0-45d6-5ef0-abbc-dcff80484059" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-276764/field-1/75d591cab066a89426c20e8dd31ecca8224da9661d1e56a33a0e42f85d2e1846" :answer-field/choices ["q-276764/field-1/75d591cab066a89426c20e8dd31ecca8224da9661d1e56a33a0e42f85d2e1846"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-276764" :question/id #uuid "34971156-0bc6-5373-b0c9-e81344239099" :question/math-academy-id "q-276764" :question/problem "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $X∼N(5,{6}^{2}),$ compute $P(X<2).$ Use the table below and do not round your answer.\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.00\\,$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,-0.6\\,$ | $\\,0.2743\\,$ | $\\,0.2709\\,$ | $\\,0.2676\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.5\\,$ | $\\,0.3085\\,$ | $\\,0.3050\\,$ | $\\,0.3015\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.4\\,$ | $\\,0.3446\\,$ | $\\,0.3409\\,$ | $\\,0.3372\\,$ |\n\n$P(X<2)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Given a normal random variable $X∼N(\\mu ,{\\sigma }^{2}),$ we have\n\n$$\nP(X<x)=P(Z<\\frac{x-\\mu }{\\sigma })\n$$\n\nwhere $Z∼N(0,1)$ is a standard normal random variable. In our case, we have $\\mu =5$ and $\\sigma =6.$\n\nFirst, we transform $X$ into a standard normal random variable $Z$ by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<2) & =P(Z<\\frac{2-5}{6}) \\\\  & =P(Z<-0.5) \\\\  & =P(Z\\le -0.5) \\\\  & =Φ(-0.5)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070250/assets/6d13179aa11fed4255ce0997c71063a6398fdbb9c6124a4048c9a29759317ab8.png)\n\nAccording to the table, we have\n\n$$\nΦ(-0.5)=0.3085.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\nP(X<2)=0.3085.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-276764/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "98bd56e8-77ca-553a-9c26-04feae0618dd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-276764"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-131541/selection/cd1db9022ef37f415df62a6b403ec48e83237f7e6831369b33fcaf509398a92d" :answer/id #uuid "0e81fed1-8798-504e-ab2f-76c1603ca300" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.1251" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131541/selection/fb9ce881860382142cc072ac5804371cd7f794955c6066444b02f08349129844" :answer/id #uuid "f2db480f-4027-5769-be22-026c2780ea0d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.1469" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131541/selection/b51907b555935fe267458d7ffd788fe7f2e4456c71d0d852884033743b5a44d8" :answer/id #uuid "e23c75b7-505d-5a93-b932-552fb7b1c67c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.1711" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131541/selection/6c7ddbcf39a9632292be94a94ad4cb818b74acdd76c690a66d1298d2be4f98d6" :answer/id #uuid "058a186d-fc9c-581f-9ee5-46b8eeedb7b3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.1230" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131541/selection/956a00ca7558b43efe8169d2d2c541d4a4548f022181809c0879da9d69a2a7cf" :answer/id #uuid "c2685d1d-9220-5c92-89b7-0e412180e7f0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.1210" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131541/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8e4f8b9b-3d2d-5c28-a5e1-96603821e8fb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-131541/selection/956a00ca7558b43efe8169d2d2c541d4a4548f022181809c0879da9d69a2a7cf" :answer-field/choices ["q-131541/selection/cd1db9022ef37f415df62a6b403ec48e83237f7e6831369b33fcaf509398a92d" "q-131541/selection/fb9ce881860382142cc072ac5804371cd7f794955c6066444b02f08349129844" "q-131541/selection/b51907b555935fe267458d7ffd788fe7f2e4456c71d0d852884033743b5a44d8" "q-131541/selection/6c7ddbcf39a9632292be94a94ad4cb818b74acdd76c690a66d1298d2be4f98d6" "q-131541/selection/956a00ca7558b43efe8169d2d2c541d4a4548f022181809c0879da9d69a2a7cf"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-131541" :question/id #uuid "eedc1079-d744-5264-956d-2ac3d0d98713" :question/math-academy-id "q-131541" :question/problem "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $X∼N(0,{10}^{2}),$ compute $P(X<-11.7).$\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ | $\\,0.06\\,$ | $\\,0.07\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,-1.1\\,$ | $\\,0.1251\\,$ | $\\,0.1230\\,$ | $\\,0.1210\\,$ |\n| $\\,-1.0\\,$ | $\\,0.1469\\,$ | $\\,0.1446\\,$ | $\\,0.1423\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.9\\,$ | $\\,0.1711\\,$ | $\\,0.1685\\,$ | $\\,0.1660\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "Given a normal random variable $X∼N(\\mu ,{\\sigma }^{2}),$ we have\n\n$$\nP(X<x)=P(Z<\\frac{x-\\mu }{\\sigma })\n$$\n\nwhere $Z∼N(0,1)$ is a standard normal random variable. In our case, we have $\\mu =0$ and $\\sigma =10.$\n\nFirst, we transform $X$ into a standard normal random variable $Z$ by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<-11.7) & =P(Z<\\frac{-11.7-0}{10}) \\\\  & =P(Z<-1.17) \\\\  & =P(Z\\le -1.17) \\\\  & =Φ(-1.17)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070250/assets/9b47010de67e748c75465b0ad1ec54d984ec7eaac6721ae9fb9b11cb60c16b16.png)\n\nAccording to the table, we have\n\n$$\nΦ(-1.17)=0.1210.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\nP(X<-11.7)=0.1210.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-131541/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "98bd56e8-77ca-553a-9c26-04feae0618dd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-131541"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-337167/field-1/8405bf9222472dac916bab5b95860a88433da01f9d6e27a83bb26d05de4dec24" :answer/id #uuid "3c5edaab-2dc5-5b47-bb53-697b40115df9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.9599" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337167/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "ddc47b99-fe84-5f34-82d0-28829ce29f0c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-337167/field-1/8405bf9222472dac916bab5b95860a88433da01f9d6e27a83bb26d05de4dec24" :answer-field/choices ["q-337167/field-1/8405bf9222472dac916bab5b95860a88433da01f9d6e27a83bb26d05de4dec24"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-337167" :question/id #uuid "2eb7e5dc-0670-546b-bad1-c9cbf061a467" :question/math-academy-id "q-337167" :question/problem "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $X∼N(3,{6}^{2}),$ compute $P(X<13.5).$ Use the table below and do not round your answer.\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ | $\\,0.06\\,$ | $\\,0.07\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,1.6\\,$ | $\\,0.9505\\,$ | $\\,0.9515\\,$ | $\\,0.9525\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.7\\,$ | $\\,0.9599\\,$ | $\\,0.9608\\,$ | $\\,0.9616\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.8\\,$ | $\\,0.9678\\,$ | $\\,0.9686\\,$ | $\\,0.9693\\,$ |\n\n$P(X<13.5)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Given a normal random variable $X∼N(\\mu ,{\\sigma }^{2}),$ we have\n\n$$\nP(X<x)=P(Z<\\frac{x-\\mu }{\\sigma })\n$$\n\nwhere $Z∼N(0,1)$ is a standard normal random variable. In our case, we have $\\mu =3$ and $\\sigma =6.$\n\nFirst, we transform $X$ into a standard normal random variable $Z$ by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<13.5) & =P(Z<\\frac{13.5-3}{6}) \\\\  & =P(Z<1.75) \\\\  & =P(Z\\le 1.75) \\\\  & =Φ(1.75)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070250/assets/e024a5ac6bdd86c88c6ed6cbe3a647281c63e6934c3830288fa01c1d51997e4a.png)\n\nAccording to the table, we have\n\n$$\nΦ(1.75)=0.9599.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\nP(X<13.5)=0.9599.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-337167/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "98bd56e8-77ca-553a-9c26-04feae0618dd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-337167"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-335886/field-1/c4e163accf83edcf62c1202195fe563c378f66d61399dc5129497bc65ecf2fa0" :answer/id #uuid "dbfd2ad1-6682-5512-a346-8257ae277762" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.7324" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335886/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "b8cb90e3-21ba-5b4f-87f8-dec937940ca2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-335886/field-1/c4e163accf83edcf62c1202195fe563c378f66d61399dc5129497bc65ecf2fa0" :answer-field/choices ["q-335886/field-1/c4e163accf83edcf62c1202195fe563c378f66d61399dc5129497bc65ecf2fa0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-335886" :question/id #uuid "37ce9b44-7ef1-5943-b6f5-144d0edbcd47" :question/math-academy-id "q-335886" :question/problem "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $Y∼N(-2,{4}^{2}),$ compute $P(Y\\ge -4.48).$ Use the table below and do not round your answer.\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.00\\,$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,-0.7\\,$ | $\\,0.2420\\,$ | $\\,0.2389\\,$ | $\\,0.2358\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.6\\,$ | $\\,0.2743\\,$ | $\\,0.2709\\,$ | $\\,0.2676\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.5\\,$ | $\\,0.3085\\,$ | $\\,0.3050\\,$ | $\\,0.3015\\,$ |\n\n$P(Y\\ge -4.48)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Given a normal random variable $Y∼N(\\mu ,{\\sigma }^{2}),$ we have\n\n$$\nP(Y\\ge y)=P(Z\\ge \\frac{y-\\mu }{\\sigma })\n$$\n\nwhere $Z∼N(0,1)$ is a standard normal random variable. In our case, we have $\\mu =-2$ and $\\sigma =4.$\n\nFirst, we transform $Y$ into a standard normal random variable $Z$ by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y\\ge -4.48) & =P(Z\\ge \\frac{-4.48-(-2)}{4}) \\\\  & =P(Z\\ge -0.62).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070250/assets/2547a2e847c503d8cdf6c2df258edd7c51e1478185f2cb0055f72425ed6fd04e.png)\n\nNow, we express the required probability in terms of $Φ(z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Z\\ge -0.62) & =1-P(Z<-0.62) \\\\  & =1-P(Z\\le -0.62) \\\\  & =1-Φ(-0.62).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the table, we know that\n\n$$\nΦ(-0.62)=0.2676.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Z\\ge -0.62) & =1-Φ(-0.62) \\\\  & =1-0.2676 \\\\  & =0.7324.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we conclude that\n\n$$\nP(Y\\ge -4.48)=0.7324.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-335886/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9b6aec2d-db43-5ff5-bd1f-1d5b38bde7e6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-335886"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-276365/field-1/a431c38c8aa764cf2c7f3df4f22da8c0af6007c784369dea64e6fd3a94f4a72f" :answer/id #uuid "1d14fcbe-0f00-57ef-8441-1db9cda2a6b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.1587" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-276365/field-1/1c590842750b502a990400eb9caadcae4a88c9c9be89113b1501e132c34ec743" :answer/id #uuid "8cd4ac18-1cc2-54b8-b33c-64ba113ba71d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.8413" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-276365/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "c258a505-630b-5534-9409-2e6656dec7d5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type 