9512c5d4ba5f568e3462f85cc25288f55a45bd5" "q-131676/selection/0f5f6291e9bd3dc451686fc26f0cb01d457f1cac289e255b985e782b044667e9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-131676" :question/id #uuid "2d84bcbe-db12-5f4f-9193-c0145f2e542f" :question/math-academy-id "q-131676" :question/problem "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $Y∼N(0,{6}^{2}),$ compute $P(Y\\ge 12.18).$\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.03\\,$ | $\\,0.04\\,$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,2.0\\,$ | $\\,0.9788\\,$ | $\\,0.9793\\,$ | $\\,0.9798\\,$ |\n| $\\,2.1\\,$ | $\\,0.9834\\,$ | $\\,0.9838\\,$ | $\\,0.9842\\,$ |\n| $\\,2.2\\,$ | $\\,0.9871\\,$ | $\\,0.9875\\,$ | $\\,0.9878\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "Given a normal random variable $Y∼N(\\mu ,{\\sigma }^{2}),$ we have\n\n$$\nP(Y\\ge y)=P(Z\\ge \\frac{y-\\mu }{\\sigma })\n$$\n\nwhere $Z∼N(0,1)$ is a standard normal random variable. In our case, we have $\\mu =0$ and $\\sigma =6.$\n\nFirst, we transform $Y$ into a standard normal random variable $Z$ by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y\\ge 12.18) & =P(Z\\ge \\frac{12.18-0}{6}) \\\\  & =P(Z\\ge 2.03)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070250/assets/c7af386057d2fba19697c0ad87c93a1865c69efaa1a5134f50bff6c7b9143dbe.png)\n\nNow, we express the required probability in terms of $Φ(z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Z\\ge 2.03) & =1-P(Z<2.03) \\\\  & =1-P(Z\\le 2.03) \\\\  & =1-Φ(2.03)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the table, we know that\n\n$$\nΦ(2.03)=0.9788.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Z\\ge 2.03) & =1-Φ(2.03) \\\\  & =1-0.9788 \\\\  & =0.0212.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we conclude that\n\n$$\nP(Y\\ge 12.18)=0.0212.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-131676/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9b6aec2d-db43-5ff5-bd1f-1d5b38bde7e6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-131676"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-336847/field-1/41fa11a75358ab0e60eeeacc744615e91da9875e2e4e8aea80b9d307f0090ac4" :answer/id #uuid "ac92124e-ce12-5414-ac20-9223e965a3a2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.4172" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336847/field-1/1e98fd4fcdb675ee2acbb7f5c510bc6e937bb132fa44bf33ad6b9b7fe46059ea" :answer/id #uuid "f15dc623-f1d0-5a74-85fe-9f0eafdb4ca4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.9808" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336847/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "11afc10f-a0ba-5218-b41b-fca307cd4a60" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-336847/field-1/41fa11a75358ab0e60eeeacc744615e91da9875e2e4e8aea80b9d307f0090ac4" :answer-field/choices ["q-336847/field-1/41fa11a75358ab0e60eeeacc744615e91da9875e2e4e8aea80b9d307f0090ac4" "q-336847/field-1/1e98fd4fcdb675ee2acbb7f5c510bc6e937bb132fa44bf33ad6b9b7fe46059ea"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-336847" :question/id #uuid "0d44ec38-49c3-5035-8f07-fc8205dd1552" :question/math-academy-id "q-336847" :question/problem "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $X∼N(10,{4}^{2}),$ compute $P(10.64<X<18.28).$ Use the tables below and do not round your answer.\n\n| | $z$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ | $\\,0.06\\,$ | $\\,0.07\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,0.1\\,$ | $\\,0.5596\\,$ | $\\,0.5636\\,$ | $\\,0.5675\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.2\\,$ | $\\,0.5987\\,$ | $\\,0.6026\\,$ | $\\,0.6064\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.3\\,$ | $\\,0.6368\\,$ | $\\,0.6406\\,$ | $\\,0.6443\\,$ | |  | | $z$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ | $\\,0.06\\,$ | $\\,0.07\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,2.0\\,$ | $\\,0.9798\\,$ | $\\,0.9803\\,$ | $\\,0.9808\\,$ |\n| $\\,2.1\\,$ | $\\,0.9842\\,$ | $\\,0.9846\\,$ | $\\,0.9850\\,$ |\n| $\\,2.2\\,$ | $\\,0.9878\\,$ | $\\,0.9881\\,$ | $\\,0.9884\\,$ | |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $z$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ | $\\,0.06\\,$ | $\\,0.07\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.1\\,$ | $\\,0.5596\\,$ | $\\,0.5636\\,$ | $\\,0.5675\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.2\\,$ | $\\,0.5987\\,$ | $\\,0.6026\\,$ | $\\,0.6064\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.3\\,$ | $\\,0.6368\\,$ | $\\,0.6406\\,$ | $\\,0.6443\\,$ |\n| $z$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ | $\\,0.06\\,$ | $\\,0.07\\,$ |\n| $\\,2.0\\,$ | $\\,0.9798\\,$ | $\\,0.9803\\,$ | $\\,0.9808\\,$ |\n| $\\,2.1\\,$ | $\\,0.9842\\,$ | $\\,0.9846\\,$ | $\\,0.9850\\,$ |\n| $\\,2.2\\,$ | $\\,0.9878\\,$ | $\\,0.9881\\,$ | $\\,0.9884\\,$ |\n\n$P(10.64<X<18.28)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Given a normal random variable $X∼N(\\mu ,{\\sigma }^{2}),$ we have\n\n$$\nP(a<X<b)=P(\\frac{a-\\mu }{\\sigma }<Z<\\frac{b-\\mu }{\\sigma })\n$$\n\nwhere $Z∼N(0,1)$ is a standard normal random variable. In our case, we have $\\mu =10$ and $\\sigma =4.$\n\nFirst, we transform $X$ into a standard normal random variable $Z$ by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(10.64<X<18.28) & =P(\\frac{10.64-10}{4}<Z<\\frac{18.28-10}{4}) \\\\  & =P(0.16<Z<2.07).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070250/assets/dc1c1e8b01372821c4ad13bfb1bbfd2a102bb9d247815ace25219d3a3f42c8c2.png)\n\nNow, we express the required probability in terms of $Φ(z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(0.16<Z<2.07) & =P(Z<2.07)-P(Z\\le 0.16) \\\\  & =P(Z\\le 2.07)-P(Z\\le 0.16) \\\\  & =Φ(2.07)-Φ(0.16).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the table, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(2.07) & =0.9808 \\\\ Φ(0.16) & =0.5636\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(0.16<Z<2.07) & =Φ(2.07)-Φ(0.16) \\\\  & =0.9808-0.5636 \\\\  & =0.4172.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we conclude that\n\n$$\nP(10.64<X<18.28)=0.4172.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-336847/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "af01940d-f4ef-53a2-b7e6-3ac45a9beb0c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-336847"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-337164/field-1/901bac163d87b473083704c4640413d8bf5efde87c523d544975294cef142c2e" :answer/id #uuid "e6b42ee1-ded7-5130-90b2-9820cb2e4065" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.8694" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337164/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "03543625-155c-5422-8957-6fdbb0c89c1a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-337164/field-1/901bac163d87b473083704c4640413d8bf5efde87c523d544975294cef142c2e" :answer-field/choices ["q-337164/field-1/901bac163d87b473083704c4640413d8bf5efde87c523d544975294cef142c2e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-337164" :question/id #uuid "ef524b79-6ad8-5245-9167-34b6ae9a0769" :question/math-academy-id "q-337164" :question/problem "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $X∼N(5,{10}^{2}),$ compute $P(-18.4<X<16.7).$\n\n| | $z$ | $\\,0.03\\,$ | $\\,0.04\\,$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,-2.4\\,$ | $\\,0.0075\\,$ | $\\,0.0073\\,$ | $\\,0.0071\\,$ |\n| $\\,-2.3\\,$ | $\\,0.0099\\,$ | $\\,0.0096\\,$ | $\\,0.0094\\,$ |\n| $\\,-2.2\\,$ | $\\,0.0129\\,$ | $\\,0.0125\\,$ | $\\,0.0122\\,$ | |  | | $z$ | $\\,0.07\\,$ | $\\,0.08\\,$ | $\\,0.09\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,1.0\\,$ | $\\,0.8577\\,$ | $\\,0.8599\\,$ | $\\,0.8621\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.1\\,$ | $\\,0.8790\\,$ | $\\,0.8810\\,$ | $\\,0.8830\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.2\\,$ | $\\,0.8980\\,$ | $\\,0.8997\\,$ | $\\,0.9015\\,$ | |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $z$ | $\\,0.03\\,$ | $\\,0.04\\,$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ |\n| $\\,-2.4\\,$ | $\\,0.0075\\,$ | $\\,0.0073\\,$ | $\\,0.0071\\,$ |\n| $\\,-2.3\\,$ | $\\,0.0099\\,$ | $\\,0.0096\\,$ | $\\,0.0094\\,$ |\n| $\\,-2.2\\,$ | $\\,0.0129\\,$ | $\\,0.0125\\,$ | $\\,0.0122\\,$ |\n| $z$ | $\\,0.07\\,$ | $\\,0.08\\,$ | $\\,0.09\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.0\\,$ | $\\,0.8577\\,$ | $\\,0.8599\\,$ | $\\,0.8621\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.1\\,$ | $\\,0.8790\\,$ | $\\,0.8810\\,$ | $\\,0.8830\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.2\\,$ | $\\,0.8980\\,$ | $\\,0.8997\\,$ | $\\,0.9015\\,$ |\n\n$P(-18.4<X<16.7)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Given a normal random variable $X∼N(\\mu ,{\\sigma }^{2}),$ we have\n\n$$\nP(a<X<b)=P(\\frac{a-\\mu }{\\sigma }<Z<\\frac{b-\\mu }{\\sigma })\n$$\n\nwhere $Z∼N(0,1)$ is a standard normal random variable. In our case, we have $\\mu =5$ and $\\sigma =10.$\n\nFirst, we transform $X$ into a standard normal random variable $Z$ by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-18.4<X<16.7) & =P(\\frac{-18.4-5}{10}<Z<\\frac{16.7-5}{10}) \\\\  & =P(-2.34<Z<1.17)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070250/assets/82e4ea3088176bbd9b03b7baa6aaa9389f21f9e9a286fa223d47bfae4252ccb6.png)\n\nNow, we express the required probability in terms of $Φ(z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-2.34<Z<1.17) & =P(Z<1.17)-P(Z\\le -2.34) \\\\  & =P(Z\\le 1.17)-P(Z\\le -2.34) \\\\  & =Φ(1.17)-Φ(-2.34)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the table, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(-2.34) & =0.0096 \\\\ Φ(1.17) & =0.8790\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-2.34<Z<1.17) & =Φ(1.17)-Φ(-2.34) \\\\  & =0.8790-0.0096 \\\\  & =0.8694.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we conclude that\n\n$$\nP(-18.4<X<16.7)=0.8694.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-337164/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "af01940d-f4ef-53a2-b7e6-3ac45a9beb0c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-337164"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-94327/selection/d82090804c683d10a345d3e59907bf5d1b0b36369d0c0922d4776d1f77