m the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $X∼N(4,{6}^{2}),$ compute $P(-3.2<X<2.86).$\n\n| | $z$ | $\\,0.00\\,$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,-1.3\\,$ | $\\,0.0968\\,$ | $\\,0.0951\\,$ | $\\,0.0934\\,$ |\n| $\\,-1.2\\,$ | $\\,0.1151\\,$ | $\\,0.1131\\,$ | $\\,0.1112\\,$ |\n| $\\,-1.1\\,$ | $\\,0.1357\\,$ | $\\,0.1335\\,$ | $\\,0.1314\\,$ | |  | | $z$ | $\\,0.07\\,$ | $\\,0.08\\,$ | $\\,0.09\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,-0.3\\,$ | $\\,0.3557\\,$ | $\\,0.3520\\,$ | $\\,0.3483\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.2\\,$ | $\\,0.3936\\,$ | $\\,0.3897\\,$ | $\\,0.3859\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.1\\,$ | $\\,0.4325\\,$ | $\\,0.4286\\,$ | $\\,0.4247\\,$ | |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $z$ | $\\,0.00\\,$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ |\n| $\\,-1.3\\,$ | $\\,0.0968\\,$ | $\\,0.0951\\,$ | $\\,0.0934\\,$ |\n| $\\,-1.2\\,$ | $\\,0.1151\\,$ | $\\,0.1131\\,$ | $\\,0.1112\\,$ |\n| $\\,-1.1\\,$ | $\\,0.1357\\,$ | $\\,0.1335\\,$ | $\\,0.1314\\,$ |\n| $z$ | $\\,0.07\\,$ | $\\,0.08\\,$ | $\\,0.09\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.3\\,$ | $\\,0.3557\\,$ | $\\,0.3520\\,$ | $\\,0.3483\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.2\\,$ | $\\,0.3936\\,$ | $\\,0.3897\\,$ | $\\,0.3859\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.1\\,$ | $\\,0.4325\\,$ | $\\,0.4286\\,$ | $\\,0.4247\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "Given a normal random variable $X∼N(\\mu ,{\\sigma }^{2}),$ we have\n\n$$\nP(a<X<b)=P(\\frac{a-\\mu }{\\sigma }<Z<\\frac{b-\\mu }{\\sigma })\n$$\n\nwhere $Z∼N(0,1)$ is a standard normal random variable. In our case, we have $\\mu =4$ and $\\sigma =6.$\n\nFirst, we transform $X$ into a standard normal random variable $Z$ by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-3.2<X<2.86) & =P(\\frac{-3.2-4}{6}<Z<\\frac{2.86-4}{6}) \\\\  & =P(-1.2<Z<-0.19)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070250/assets/1ed2c43f507a4d0ddd54126bcd3efaa2fa9b56c63ea908e8567e6959e3fc67bc.png)\n\nNow, we express the required probability in terms of $Φ(z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-1.2<Z<-0.19) & =P(Z<-0.19)-P(Z\\le -1.2) \\\\  & =P(Z\\le -0.19)-P(Z\\le -1.2) \\\\  & =Φ(-0.19)-Φ(-1.2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the table, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(-1.2) & =0.1151 \\\\ Φ(-0.19) & =0.4247\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-1.2<Z<-0.19) & =Φ(-0.19)-Φ(-1.2) \\\\  & =0.4247-0.1151 \\\\  & =0.3096.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we conclude that\n\n$$\nP(-3.2<X<2.86)=0.3096.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-94327/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "af01940d-f4ef-53a2-b7e6-3ac45a9beb0c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-94327"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-94319"] :question/problem "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $X∼N(2,25),$ compute $P(-0.65<X<-0.25).$\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.03\\,$ | $\\,0.04\\,$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,-0.5\\,$ | $\\,0.2981\\,$ | $\\,0.2946\\,$ | $\\,0.2912\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.4\\,$ | $\\,0.3336\\,$ | $\\,0.3300\\,$ | $\\,0.3264\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.3\\,$ | $\\,0.3707\\,$ | $\\,0.3669\\,$ | $\\,0.3632\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "Given a normal random variable $X∼N(\\mu ,{\\sigma }^{2}),$ we have\n\n$$\nP(a<X<b)=P(\\frac{a-\\mu }{\\sigma }<Z<\\frac{b-\\mu }{\\sigma })\n$$\n\nwhere $Z∼N(0,1)$ is a standard normal random variable. In our case, we have $\\mu =2$ and $\\sigma =\\sqrt{25}=5.$\n\nFirst, we transform $X$ into a standard normal random variable $Z$ by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-0.65<X<-0.25) & =P(\\frac{-0.65-2}{5}<Z<\\frac{-0.25-2}{5}) \\\\  & =P(-0.53<Z<-0.45)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070250/assets/3d73cc4661eb9f68f636803918b3e55942e6538e4e70d13277d125386dad257e.png)\n\nNow, we express the required probability in terms of $Φ(z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-0.53<Z<-0.45) & =P(Z<-0.45)-P(Z\\le -0.53) \\\\  & =P(Z\\le -0.45)-P(Z\\le -0.53) \\\\  & =Φ(-0.45)-Φ(-0.53)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the table, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(-0.53) & =0.2981 \\\\ Φ(-0.45) & =0.3264\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-0.53<Z<-0.45) & =Φ(-0.45)-Φ(-0.53) \\\\  & =0.3264-0.2981 \\\\  & =0.0283.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we conclude that\n\n$$\nP(-0.65<X<-0.25)=0.0283.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-94318/selection/f93f9821329a076a75726588b2095206f1b931ebf999c04ce581793265fc96ef" :answer/id #uuid "ff545fbe-f8f9-5d67-9582-e0e6812e1de7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.2299" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94318/selection/4492617ca352f99491a75223fbba8f0d1b1dbcca035bd290bef13b73eb769ec8" :answer/id #uuid "82bebcca-0033-56d8-9eba-b5f8bf78d7c3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.2380" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94318/selection/76db4264b81d304752713cd8cc35cf3ffedfc0821e709ad4c03c48e409a17ec9" :answer/id #uuid "585d832c-0703-50fd-9166-1c0fb4a9171e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.2812" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94318/selection/ae6919d7fb9bf557a761d2e808adf8bd80af4f6949d8676c47cff7dfc5c17299" :answer/id #uuid "d9c14a9d-6908-5ac7-8987-305a0bce8053" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.2290" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94318/selection/fab50fd68cbb737ac01c2605137aed0bdd0aba94d93f74ae21a47af9705f71a1" :answer/id #uuid "19f00002-9178-550b-a945-acefb818cc63" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.2892" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94318/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b5c85319-0d0f-5b